source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Port the commits an addon has on another series and lacks on the target, grouped by pull request, on the branch `<to>-port-<addon>`

Usage: odx port addon [OPTIONS] --from <SERIES> --to <SERIES> <ADDON>

Arguments:
  <ADDON>
          Addon name

Options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

      --from <SERIES>
          Source series

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml or repos.yaml to use

      --to <SERIES>
          Target series

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --remote <NAME>
          The remote the series come from [default: the one pointing at the pull request's repository; for addons `upstream` when it exists, else `origin`]

      --no-migrate
          Leave out odoo-lint's upgrade fixes

      --offline
          Serve forge and index data from the cache only. Only network calls are skipped: local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --open-pr
          Then push the branch and open a draft pull request

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --push-remote <NAME>
          With --open-pr: push to this remote instead of the target or your fork

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version
